+# Decision: the lab is the central Scope, and which processes are kept
+
+Decided by Justin on the afternoon of 2026-10-04, in an interview. Copied on 2026-10-07 from `STATE.md` (the version
+of 2026-10-04 17:31, lines 38 to 54), which is overwritten at each verified event and was the only place these were
+recorded. Copying them here is not deciding them again; the wording is as `STATE.md` recorded it.
+
+## Decided
+
+- **The lab is the central Scope** for project management, core issue tracking, code quality and security. Astra is
+  to say what else it should cover.
+- **Where issues live:** a Scope's issues stay in its own repository, on one central map; a `core` label marks a
+  Scope issue that needs ORC's core changed. Later, Scopes may track their own business logic elsewhere.
+- **The processes kept, all of them:**
+  - map and label check;
+  - tests on every PR (#144);
+  - the security-review and package-API checks;
+  - daily diary;
+  - weekly adversarial review;
+  - entropy guard at session end;
+  - FRICTION into rules, monthly (#60);
+  - branch and worktree cleanup (#70);
+  - `/tmp` cleanup (#182).
+- **ORC scheduling (#166) is built first,** and the scheduled ones run through it.
+- **Astra runs entropy-guard's assessment on ORC and the lab together.** Justin was shaping the brief before it ran.
+
+## Also decided by Justin on 2026-10-04, recorded in `STATE.md`
+
+- **Moving Stillness is paused.** Browser-stack work that touches it (#118, #52, MS #52) waits.
